  "text": {
    "TXT_KEY_DOOM_SUNDERING": "The Sundering",
    "TXT_KEY_DOOM_SUNDERING_HELP": "Every civilization with more than 3 cities and a capital loses the quarter of its cities farthest from its capital (rounded down, at least 1), which secede as a new civilization of the same civilization type:[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Its leader: one of that civilization's leaders not in play this game; if none is free, one of its minor leaders.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]The cities keep their buildings, culture and land combat units; heroes stay with the old civilization. The most populous of them is its capital.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]It knows the old civilization's techs (not its cards) and has met every civilization it has met.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]It is no one's vassal and at peace with every civilization; led by a leader with the Barbarian trait, it is at peace with the barbarians.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]-4 attitude between it and the old civilization, both ways.[NEWLINE]Not split: the Sheaim, the Infernals, and a civilization with no free leader (the civilizations born of cards). Played only when a civilization splits.",
    "TXT_KEY_MINOR_LEADER_OF": "Minor leader: %s1 (The Sundering)",
    "TXT_KEY_LEADER_TORRIN": "Torrin Coldforge",
    "TXT_KEY_LEADER_TORRIN_PEDIA": "Torrin Coldforge kept the furnaces of the eastern holds burning through the long winters. His golems answer to him before they answer to any king.",
    "TXT_KEY_LEADER_YSOLDE": "Ysolde Lorda",
    "TXT_KEY_LEADER_YSOLDE_PEDIA": "Ysolde Lorda is Cardith's kinswoman, and holds that the Lorda name belongs to whoever rules the cities, not to whoever sits in the oldest of them.",
    "TXT_KEY_LEADER_CAELITH": "Caelith Sunbough",
    "TXT_KEY_LEADER_CAELITH_PEDIA": "Caelith Sunbough speaks for the outer groves, whose trees the court in the capital has never walked beneath.",
    "TXT_KEY_LEADER_DURGRIM": "Durgrim Deepvault",
    "TXT_KEY_LEADER_DURGRIM_PEDIA": "Durgrim Deepvault counts the gold of the far vaults, and has stopped sending it to the throne.",
    "TXT_KEY_LEADER_SELKA": "Selka Saltreach",
    "TXT_KEY_LEADER_SELKA_PEDIA": "Selka Saltreach captains the outer harbours. She pays her crews, and her crews no longer ask whose flag they sail under.",
    "TXT_KEY_LEADER_RAZIEL": "Raziel",
    "TXT_KEY_LEADER_RAZIEL_PEDIA": "Raziel was Basium's herald, until the host on the mortal side of the gate grew too large for one voice to command."
  }
}
